          "solution": "<p>Take \\(u(t)=1-t\\) and \\(v'(t)=f''(t),\\) so \\(u'=-1\\) and we may take \\(v=f'.\\) Integration by parts gives</p>\n\\[\\int_0^1(1-t)f''(t)\\,\\mathrm dt\n=\\left.(1-t)f'(t)\\right|_0^1+\\int_0^1 f'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt.\\]\n<p>The boundary term is \\(-f'(0).\\) The FTOC evaluates the remaining integral as \\(f(1)-f(0),\\) giving \\(f(1)-f(0)-f'(0).\\)</p>",
