          "solution": "<p>Set \\(\\varphi(t)=a+(b-a)t=(1-t)a+tb.\\) Then \\(\\varphi(0)=a,\\) \\(\\varphi(1)=b,\\) and \\(\\varphi'(t)=b-a&gt;0.\\) By change of variables,</p>\n\\[\\int_a^b f(x)\\,\\mathrm dx\n=\\int_0^1 f(\\varphi(t))\\,\\varphi'(t)\\,\\mathrm dt\n=(b-a)\\int_0^1 f\\bigl((1-t)a+tb\\bigr)\\,\\mathrm dt.\\]\n<p>Divide by \\(b-a\\) to obtain the identity.</p>",
